-- title:
--   Supersingular chart with Drinfeld ends, decomposition and inertia
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Fix a prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be (`hH₁`) the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; thus $H_1$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be (`hK`) the intermediate field [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of $L \subseteq L((t))$, that is, the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra through the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = qu$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` denotes the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin` $= j$; [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) denotes the scheme obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of this ring to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the analogous ring for $j^{-1}$ along the intermediate ring, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and canonical morphism `ιFin` from `XFin` $= \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin`. A maximal ideal $y$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` is fixed, containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is assumed supersingular (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $x \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $x$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   A *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$*, for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ with $p_g$ nonzero over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of the expansion of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \widetilde{\gamma^{-1}}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \widetilde{\gamma^{-1}}$, where $\widetilde{\gamma^{-1}} =$ `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/q \\ qc & d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\gamma^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} a& b\\ c& d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hArig` (completed-stalk Drinfeld chart, seven clauses).** For every point $z$ of the two-chart model at which the germ of $\varpi$ pulled back through `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`-image $z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the sense of `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, elements $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu\big)$, such that, with `toC` the completion map, `mkS` the quotient map and `germY` the germ map from `chartAlgFin A K j` to the stalk: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves `chartAlgFin A K j`; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin A K j` is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) whenever such a $\tau$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) preserves the chart and is the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ transporting $\tau$ along $e \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY`, $\theta$ fixing all constants, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ when $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) for prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, neither containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, both containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ and $a_i, b_i \in \mathbb{Z}$, with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e \circ$ `toC` are distinct; (vi) for such a prime $P$ containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a$ of the chart has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-series with constant term removed, expanded in $t^q$) lies in $K$ and in the chart, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and $e$ carries the germ of `jqNModC` $- a_0$ to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hArigI` (tame-inertia rider).** For every $z$, $y'$ as above and every $W$, $\sigma$, $f$, $u$, $v$, $e$ as in `hArig` (universally quantified) for which clause (i) and clause (iv) hold, the following is required: for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, every pair of ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A$ compatible with $A \to L$ and with $\sigma_A \equiv \mathrm{id}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$, every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every $\tilde\alpha$ with $\sigma_A\pi = \tilde\alpha\pi$ and $\tilde\alpha^{q+1} \equiv d$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (via the natural representative of $d$), and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting on Laurent expansions coefficientwise through $\sigma_L$: $\tau$ preserves `chartAlgFin A K j`; and, granted that, $\tau$ is the identity modulo $y'$ and there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$, an element $ct \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ transporting $\tau$, $\sigma_W \circ \sigma = \sigma \circ \sigma_A$, $\sigma_W \equiv \mathrm{id}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $\theta(C w) = C(\sigma_W w)$, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $ct \equiv \sigma(\tilde\alpha^{q+1})$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and $M_{ij} \equiv ct \cdot \big(\mathrm{diag}(1, (d^q)^{-1})\big)_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, the matrix being [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.diagOneElem q (d ^ q)⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L233) over $\mathbb{Z}/q$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exist an $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ and a valuation subring $W$ of $K$ (not the power-series base ring of the hypotheses) with $B \subseteq W$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) `chartAlgFin A K j` $\subseteq B$. (2) $K$ is the fraction field of $B$: every $f \in K$ is $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \neq 0$. (3) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. (4) $W \cap L = A$, in the sense that $x \in L$ has image in $W$ exactly when $x$ comes from $A$; the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; and $W$ is a discrete valuation ring. (5) For $b$ in the chart, $b \in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $W$ and in $\mathfrak{m}_W$. (6) $f \in K$ lies in $W$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   (7) For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ with: $\rho b = 0$ exactly when $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; $\rho$ restricted to $A$ the residue map followed by $k \to$ `CoordRing`; and the following equivariance. For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\overline\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (that is, $\det(\overline\gamma)\,c^{q+1} = 1$, where $\overline\gamma =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.redQ q γ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L230)) such that $\rho(\tau b) =$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325)$(\overline\gamma, c)(\rho b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau b \in B$; moreover $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; and there are $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau'$ at $\gamma'^{-1}$ preserving $W$ with $(1,c) \in$ `hSubgroup q` and $\rho(\tau' b) =$ `hAction`$(1,c)(\rho b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau' b \in B$.
--
--   (8) $B$ is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. (9) For every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ has $\tau b \in B$ and $\tau b \in Q$. (10) If $b \in B$ is such that for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ the element $\tau b$, when it lies in $B$, lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$. (11) A level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ (that is, $b \in y \leftrightarrow \tau b \in y$ for chart elements $b$ with $\tau b$ in the chart) preserves $W$.
--
--   (12) There exist: an integer $n \ge 1$ dividing $q+1$; $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W$; an integer $m \ge 1$ with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for some unit $w$; an element $\zeta_0$ of the adic completion $\widehat A$ with $\zeta_0^n = 1$ and $\zeta_0^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$; witnesses that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in the chart, together with $a_0 \in A$ such that `jqNModC` $- a_0 \in y$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$, such that: (a) $\tau_0^{\,n}$ fixes $B$ pointwise; (b) for $0 < k < n$ the map $\tau_0^{\,k}$ moves some element of $B$; (c) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ agrees on $B$ with $\tau_0^{\,k}$ for some $k < n$; (d) `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements; (e) every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ maps each $O \in$ `ends` onto some $O' \in$ `ends` ($f \in O \leftrightarrow \tau f \in O'$); (f) for any $O, O' \in$ `ends` some such $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ preserving $W$ carries $O$ onto $O'$; (g) $\tau_0$ carries each $O \in$ `ends` onto itself; (h) distinct $O, O' \in$ `ends` admit an element lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$; (i) there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K$, of finite type over $A$ and stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every $O \in$ `ends`, with each $O$ equal to the set of $f$ of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$; (j) if a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ maps some $O \in$ `ends` into $W$, it preserves $W$.
--
--   (k) Each $O \in$ `ends` satisfies: $O \subseteq W$; $O$ is local and Noetherian; the chart is contained in $O$; $O \cap L = A$; every $f \in O$ is such that $f - a$ is a non-unit of $O$ for some $a \in A$ whose image lies in $O$. Moreover the image of $\varpi$ lies in $O$ and there are $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ onto `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat A\,(\varpi^m) = \widehat A[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi^m)$, units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that ring, an $\widehat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of it, and $\zeta_0'$ with $\zeta_0\zeta_0' = 1$, the crossing model being local, such that: $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries images of elements of $A$ to the corresponding constants; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V V$; $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ and $c_x$ does not; `jqNModC` $- a_0$ lies in $O$ and $\iota$ carries it to $w_V V^{e}$ for some unit $w_V$ and some $e \ge 1$; $\iota$ intertwines $\tau_0$ with $\theta_0$ on elements of $O$ whose $\tau_0$-image lies in $O$; and $\theta_0(U) \equiv \zeta_0 U$, $\theta_0(V) \equiv \zeta_0' V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal of the crossing model. Furthermore there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K$ with $O \subseteq W_x$, containing the chart, with $W_x \cap L = A$, a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\varpi$, containing an element $t$ such that for every $p \in A[X]$ with $p(t) \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$, with the same property for `jqNModC` in place of $t$, with $c_x \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ and $c_y \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$, such that every chart element lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ lies in $y$ while some element of $y$ is a unit of $W_x$, such that every $O' \in$ `ends` other than $O$ has an element outside $W_x$, and such that no $O' \in$ `ends` is mapped into $W_x$ by a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ unless $O' = O$. Furthermore there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $K$ contained in $B \cap O$, of finite type over $A$, stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, all of whose elements have non-negative order at every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ (in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22)) at which $j$ has non-negative order, such that $O$ consists exactly of the $g/h$ with $g,h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$, and containing an element $b$ which lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L = A$, with $\varpi \in \mathfrak{m}_V$, with $j \in V$ and every monic $p \in A[X]$ having $p(j)$ a unit of $V$, and having some element of $O$ outside $V$.
--
--   (l) Every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L = A$ which contains the chart and has every element of $y$ in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ either contains $B$, or dominates one of the ends: there is $O \in$ `ends` with $O \subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ in $\mathfrak{m}_V$. (m) There is $b \in B$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with $V \cap L = A$ and $\varpi \in \mathfrak{m}_V$ such that, if $j \in V$, no monic $p \in A[X]$ has $p(j) \in \mathfrak{m}_V$. (n) For every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart containing $\varpi$ which is carried to $y$ by no level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (that is, for no such pair does $b \in y \leftrightarrow \tau b \in y''$ hold for all chart elements), there is $b \in B$ which, for all such $\gamma$ and $\tau$, lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ containing the chart with the property that each chart element $c$ with $\tau^{-1}c \in y''$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$.
--
--   (13) For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with the same three normalisations and the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance as in (7) (kernel the elements of $\mathfrak{m}_W$; compatibility with residues on $A$; the constant $c$ with $(\overline\gamma,c) \in$ `hSubgroup q`, the clause $c \neq 1$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ with $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$, and the companion $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ realising $(1,c)$), and in addition a tame-inertia law: there is $\eta \in \{1,q\}$ such that for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every pair of ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $L$, $\sigma_A$ of $A$ compatible with $A \to L$ and with $\sigma_A \equiv \mathrm{id}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$, every $\tilde\alpha$ with $\sigma_A\pi = \tilde\alpha\pi$, every $\alpha \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ whose image in $k$ is the residue of $\tilde\alpha$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting on Laurent expansions coefficientwise through $\sigma_L$: $\tau$ preserves $B$ and preserves $W$, and for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ equals $\alpha^{q+1}$, provided $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^\eta)^{-1}), \alpha^\eta) \in$ `hSubgroup q`, one has $\rho(\tau b) =$ `hAction`$(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^\eta)^{-1}), \alpha^\eta)(\rho b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau b \in B$.
--
--   This is the supersingular-point step in the construction of an integral model of the modular curve attached to the auxiliary level $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ (units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$): from the completed-stalk Drinfeld chart data it produces a global affine chart $B$ over $A$ whose special fibre is the Drinfeld curve $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 = 1$, together with the $q+1$ local rings of the ends crossing it, the valuation $W$ cutting out the Drinfeld component, the action of the deck transformations through `hSubgroup q`, and the tame-inertia law. It is the variant of the construction for arbitrary prime $q$ (no hypothesis $q \ge 5$, and the diamond condition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$ in place of a full level condition at $\ell$), and is used by the tame-hypothesis form of the same export.
